<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 111 0 R
/T (Before the browser can contact the server, it must find the server's IP address. The lookup order is: \(1\) browser cache, \(2\) operating-system cache / hosts file, \(3\) the DNS resolver of the ISP or a public DNS \(e.g. 8.8.8.8\), which, if it does not already know the answer, asks the \(4\) root server, \(5\) the .in TLD server and \(6\) the college's authoritative name server. The IP address is returned and cached.)
/E (Before the browser can contact the server, it must find the server's IP address. The lookup order is: \(1\) browser cache, \(2\) operating-system cache / hosts file, \(3\) the DNS resolver of the ISP or a public DNS \(e.g. 8.8.8.8\), which, if it does not already know the answer, asks the \(4\) root server, \(5\) the .in TLD server and \(6\) the college's authoritative name server. The IP address is returned and cached.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [12]
>>
